        'levels_h' => 'How many bars a project has', 'levels_p' => 'The three bars of the mark also say how far along a project is.',
        'help_h' => 'Something wrong?', 'help_p' => 'If you find a mistake or have an idea, write: that is how projects in testing get better.', 'help_contact' => 'Write to Saverio', 'help_code' => 'See the code of the portal',
        'privacy_title' => 'Privacy', 'privacy_desc' => 'How the Illerom portal handles the data of its visitors.', 'privacy_h1' => 'Privacy of the portal',
        'privacy' => [
            ['In two lines', 'The portal uses no cookies, has no statistics, asks for no registration and loads nothing from other sites: fonts, icons and components are all hosted here.'],
            ['Controller', 'Saverio Morelli, a private individual who runs the portal and the projects on a non-commercial basis. For any request, including to exercise your rights, use the contact form on saveriomorelli.com.'],
            ['What stays on your device', 'Only the theme, if you change it (light or dark). It is kept in the browser’s storage, is never sent, and can be deleted from the browser settings. It is strictly necessary to remember a choice of yours, so it needs no consent (art. 122 of the Italian Privacy Code and the Garante’s cookie guidelines of 10 June 2021).'],
            ['What the server receives', 'Like any site, to show you the pages the server receives your IP address, the kind of browser and your preferred language, used only to choose between Italian and English. The portal does not save them; the hosting provider may keep them in technical logs for security, for no longer than needed.'],
            ['Why and on what basis', 'To show you the portal and keep it secure: legitimate interest in running and protecting the site (art. 6.1.f GDPR). There is no profiling and no automated decision-making.'],
            ['Who receives the data', 'The hosting provider, Aruba S.p.A. (Italy), acting as processor (art. 28 GDPR). The data stays in the European Union and is never sold or handed over.'],
            ['Your rights', 'You can ask for access, rectification, erasure, restriction and portability, and object to the processing (arts. 15–22 GDPR). You can lodge a complaint with the Italian data protection authority, the Garante per la protezione dei dati personali (www.garanteprivacy.it), or go to court.'],
            ['The projects', 'Every project has its own privacy notice, linked from its page: for the data it processes, that one applies. Some ask for an account: the page says so. The terms of use of the portal apply to all of them too.'],
            ['Language', 'Only the Italian text is legally binding; this English version is a courtesy copy.'],
        ],
        'updated' => 'Last updated: 27 November 2026',
        'terms_title' => 'Terms of use', 'terms_nav' => 'Terms', 'terms_desc' => 'The common terms of use of the Illerom portal, its projects and SavOffice: who provides them, who answers for what, how to report illegal content.',
        'terms_h1' => 'Terms of use of Illerom and its projects',
        'terms' => [
            ['Language', 'Only the Italian text is legally binding; this English version is a courtesy copy and, if the two differ, the Italian text prevails.'],
            ['Who provides the services', 'The portal www.illerom.eu, the projects published on it and the SavOffice apps are provided by Saverio Morelli, a private individual, free of charge and on a non-commercial basis. Contact: the form at www.saveriomorelli.com/contact-me/.'],
            ['What they apply to', 'These terms apply to the portal and to every project. When a project has terms of its own, those apply too and, where they are more specific, they prevail. By using a project you accept these terms.'],
            ['The service', 'The projects are free, open source and provided as they are, with no guarantee of continuity or of being free of errors: some are still in testing and may change or be suspended. Keep a copy of the data that matters, which you can download where the project allows it.'],
            ['Age', 'To create an account you must be at least 14 (art. 8 GDPR and art. 2-quinquies of the Italian Privacy Code). Below that age, the consent of whoever holds parental responsibility is needed.'],
            ['Everyone answers for their own actions', 'The projects are tools: whoever provides them does not decide what is written, uploaded, shared or sent with them and does not check it beforehand. Whoever uses a service is solely responsible for their own actions with and within it: for the content they create, upload, share or send, for the people they make it visible to, for the data of other people they put in it (which they must have the right to do) and for the consequences, also towards third parties. Whoever breaches these terms or the law holds the provider harmless from the resulting third-party claims.'],
            ['Not allowed', 'Illegal, defamatory or hateful content, content inciting violence or infringing the rights of others (copyright and privacy included); material exploiting minors; phishing, fraud, collecting passwords or payment data; spam; malware; impersonating someone else; attempts to get around the security or the limits of the services or to reach other people’s data.'],
            ['Reporting illegal content', 'Anyone can report content they consider illegal or against these terms (art. 16 of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065, the Digital Services Act): with the report button of the project, where there is one, or with the contact form. Give the exact address of the content, why you consider it illegal, your name and email (except for offences against children) and a statement that the report is made in good faith. You get an acknowledgement and the decision, taken without delay by a person.'],
            ['Moderation, reasons and complaints', 'When content is removed or hidden, or an account is suspended or blocked, whoever is affected gets the reasons (art. 17 DSA): what was done, why and on what basis. Decisions are taken by people, with no automated systems. You can challenge them free of charge with the contact form, within six months; you can also turn to a certified out-of-court dispute settlement body (art. 21 DSA) or to the courts. Whoever often posts manifestly illegal content, or often sends manifestly unfounded reports, may be suspended after a warning (art. 23 DSA).'],
            ['Point of contact', 'For the authorities of the Member States, the European Commission and the people who use the services, the single point of contact (arts. 11 and 12 DSA) is the form at www.saveriomorelli.com/contact-me/, in Italian or English.'],
            ['Privacy', 'Every project has its own privacy notice, linked from its page; the portal has its own. Data is processed under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and the Italian Privacy Code (Legislative Decree 196/2003).'],
            ['Liability', 'Within the limits allowed by law, the provider is not liable for the content and actions of users, nor for damage arising from the use or unavailability of the services. Cases of wilful misconduct or gross negligence and the rights the law gives to consumers are not affected and are not limited by these terms.'],
            ['Changes and governing law', 'These terms may change; important changes are announced in the projects concerned and the date at the bottom shows the latest version. Italian law applies; for consumers, the court of their place of residence or domicile remains competent.'],
        ],
        'terms_updated' => 'Last updated: 27 November 2026',
