        'tf_nav' => 'Typeface', 'tf_title' => 'Illerom Bars, the typeface', 'tf_desc' => 'Illerom Bars: the graphic typeface born from the Illerom mark, an alphabet of crooked bars for lettering and decorations. Try it, download it and use it freely.',
        'tf_h1' => 'A *crooked* alphabet, one bar at a time.',
        'tf_lede' => 'Illerom Bars comes from the mark: each letter is reduced to its main strokes, drawn with bars on an upright grid and then leaned. It is a graphic typeface, like the mark: for lettering, titles and decorations, not for text to be read (for that the site uses Inter).',
        'tf_try_h' => 'Try writing', 'tf_try_label' => 'Your text', 'tf_sample' => 'open projects, even the slightly crooked ones', 'tf_lean' => 'Lean', 'tf_lean_labels' => 'Upright, Crooked',
        'tf_preview' => 'The text written in Illerom Bars', 'tf_mono' => 'Monospaced', 'tf_mono_help' => 'Every letter in a cell of its own: ill no longer looks like m', 'tf_play' => 'Write again',
        'tf_alpha_h' => 'The alphabet', 'tf_alpha_p' => 'Capitals and small letters are the same. The digits are built like letters: 0 like O, 1 like I, 2 like S, 3 and 5 like E, 4, 7 and 9 like Q, 6 like R, 8 like X. Hover over a letter, or tap it, to straighten it.',
        'tf_rules_h' => 'How it is made',
        'tf_rules' => [['An upright grid', 'Each letter sits on a grid 100 tall: bars 15 thick, 16 apart inside a letter and 27 between letters.'], ['Stems or lines, never both', 'Each letter is made only of upright stems or only of horizontal lines. There are at most three stems, each whole, only its top half or only its bottom half. There are at most three lines (top, middle, bottom), all of one length.'], ['Then it leans', 'In the end everything leans one step every two, as in the mark. The LEAN axis goes from 0 (upright) to 100 (crooked), and it can be animated.']],
        'tf_twins_h' => 'Twin letters', 'tf_twins_p' => 'As in the mark, where i and l are the same bar, some letters coincide on purpose. It is not a flaw: Illerom Bars is for drawing words, not for reading them.',
        'tf_get_h' => 'Use it', 'tf_get_p' => 'There are two families: Illerom Bars, where the letters close up as in the mark, and Illerom Bars Mono, where each one has a cell of its own. The package has every format and the MIT licence, the same as the portal: OTF, crooked and upright, for writing and design apps; variable TTF, with the LEAN axis, for recent apps; WOFF for websites.',
